# 3. Official Agent Naming Convention

All agent IDs must follow this format:

`AGT-001` through `AGT-029`

The official agent names must follow this format:

`[Business Category] Agent`

Examples:

- General Retail Agent.
- Restaurant Agent.
- Pharmacy Agent.

Each agent must have:

- Permanent ID.
- Official name.
- Assigned category ID.
- Category name.
- Unique registry record.
- Version number.

Agent IDs must never be reused for another category.

If an agent's official name changes in the future, its permanent ID and category assignment must remain unchanged unless a formally approved registry revision explicitly authorizes reassignment.

