# 8. Registry Governance

The master registry must be treated as a controlled architectural document.

The following rules apply:

1. Agent IDs are permanent identifiers.
2. Category mapping is one-to-one.
3. Agent responsibilities must remain category-specific.
4. Duplicate agent definitions are prohibited.
5. Unrestricted cross-category operations are prohibited.
6. Tenant isolation is mandatory.
7. Existing GeFlow modules remain the operational source of truth.
8. Shared infrastructure is permitted.
9. Agent configurations and permissions must remain isolated.
10. Agent versions must be tracked.
11. Registry changes require explicit authorization.
12. Every approved change must include a reason and impact assessment.
13. Deprecated agents must not silently disappear from historical records.
14. Registry changes must not automatically change the running application.
15. Documentation finalization must not be treated as deployment authorization.

